// Individually edited introductions. Keep the full researched article below each answer.
const copy = [
 ['riseklix-vs-clipping-net-india','Compare the workflow, campaign rules and support you need before choosing RiseKlix or Clipping.net.','Compare RiseKlix and Clipping.net by how a campaign is run, not just by the name. Check source permissions, review rules, payment conditions and who handles questions. RiseKlix is a managed, Discord-first network. Use each provider’s current information to confirm what is available; this guide is not an independent ranking.'],
 ['riseklix-vs-whop-clips-india','Understand the difference between a managed RiseKlix campaign and clipping offers available through Whop.','RiseKlix and Whop serve different roles. RiseKlix runs a managed clipping network; Whop hosts products and communities whose campaign rules can differ. For an Indian campaign, compare the actual offer, permitted content, review process, fees and supported payment methods. A platform listing alone does not confirm work or earnings.'],
 ['riseklix-vs-vyro-india','Compare campaign management, account requirements and payment rules for an India-focused clipping campaign.','Choose between RiseKlix and Vyro by checking the campaign you can actually join or run. Compare approved sources, publishing accounts, review responsibilities, payment rules and support. RiseKlix uses a managed, Discord-first workflow. Confirm Vyro’s current offer directly; a familiar brand name does not tell you all the campaign conditions.'],
 ['riseklix-vs-makeclout-india','Check current provider information and compare campaign scope, review and payment conditions.','Start by checking the provider’s current name and offer: MakeClout has been presented as Clouted in the information reviewed for this guide. Then compare it with RiseKlix on campaign scope, permissions, review, payment conditions and support. Treat this as a decision checklist, not proof that either service will produce better results.'],
 ['best-clipping-platforms-india','A practical checklist for comparing clipping platforms, communities and managed services in India.','The best clipping platform for you depends on whether you want editing work, a community or someone to manage a campaign. Check source rights, clear approval rules, payment terms, Indian payment support and an accessible support route. Compare current offers against those needs rather than relying on a single ranked list.'],
 ['clipconnect-india-alternative','Compare alternatives by the work you need done, the review process and the terms you can confirm.','If you are looking for a ClipConnect alternative in India, first decide what you need: campaign management, editing work or a place to find participants. Compare current providers on permissions, deliverables, review, payment and support. RiseKlix is one managed-network option to discuss with the team; availability and scope need confirming.'],
 ['creator-clipping-agency-vs-clipping-marketplace','Decide who should manage the brief, find editors, review clips and handle campaign questions.','A clipping agency usually takes on agreed campaign work and management. A marketplace helps people find offers or participants, with responsibilities depending on the provider and campaign. Choose based on who will write the brief, review edits, handle questions and confirm payments. The service label alone does not settle those responsibilities.'],
 ['discord-clipping-network-vs-saas-clipping-platform','Compare a community-led workflow with a software platform, including review records and support.','A Discord clipping network coordinates people through a community. A software platform may provide forms, account connections or dashboards. Either needs clear source permissions, approval rules, payment terms and support. Compare how the actual workflow handles submissions and corrections; having a dashboard or a large server does not prove campaign quality.'],
 ['managed-clipping-campaign-vs-hiring-freelance-editors','Compare management time, editing scope, review and cost before choosing how to run a campaign.','Hiring freelance editors gives you direct control over their agreed editing work, while you may still need to organise sources, reviews and publishing. A managed clipping campaign can combine those tasks within its agreed scope. Compare the full workload and cost, including revisions and reporting, rather than only the price of an edit.'],
 ['riseklix-vs-traditional-social-media-agency','Understand where a clipping campaign fits alongside broader social media management.','RiseKlix focuses on managed clipping campaigns using approved source content. A social media agency may cover a wider set of tasks, such as planning posts, community management or paid media. Compare the written scope with the work you need. Neither model automatically includes every channel, service or business result.'],
 ['riseklix-vs-influencer-marketing-agency-india','Compare repurposing your content with commissioning an influencer to create and publish new content.','A clipping campaign turns approved videos into short edits. An influencer campaign usually commissions content or promotion through an influencer’s account. Compare source ownership, who creates and publishes the work, disclosure, review and the result you want to measure. RiseKlix’s clipping workflow may suit one part of that plan; confirm the scope with the team.'],
 ['how-to-become-a-clipper-india','Learn the basics, prepare samples you have permission to make and join the RiseKlix Discord community.','To become a clipper in India, learn to choose useful video moments, edit them clearly and add accurate captions. Build a few samples using content you have permission to use. Join a campaign community, read its brief and confirm approval and payment rules before working. Joining RiseKlix Discord is the first step here; work is not guaranteed.'],
 ['how-much-do-clippers-make-india','Understand rates, eligible views, fees and payment caps before estimating your clipper earnings.','There is no verified national salary figure for Indian clippers in this guide. Earnings depend on the campaign’s agreed payment model, accepted work, eligible views, fees and caps. Use the written terms to estimate a scenario, then separate that estimate from money approved or paid. Public view counts alone do not confirm earnings.'],
 ['clipping-side-hustle-india','Work out whether clipping fits your skills, available time and the campaign terms you can confirm.','Clipping can be a side activity if you have time to learn editing, check sources and handle revisions. Before accepting work, confirm the deliverables, approval process, rate and payment schedule. Track your time and costs as well as payments. Treat it as work with variable availability, not a guaranteed income stream.'],
 ['freelance-clipper-guide-india','Prepare a portfolio, agree a clear scope and keep useful records from brief to payment.','A freelance clipper needs more than editing software. Prepare samples you have permission to use, agree what you will deliver and confirm deadlines, revisions and payment in writing. Keep the brief, submitted files and review decisions together. This makes questions easier to resolve and helps you judge whether the work fits your time.'],
 ['remote-clipping-jobs-india','Check a remote clipping offer, prepare relevant samples and understand the terms before accepting work.','For remote clipping work, look for a clear brief, an identifiable team and written payment conditions. Ask which content you may use, where clips will be published and how approval works. Prepare relevant samples and keep your submission records. A Discord invite or advertised earning figure alone does not confirm a paid role.'],
 ['best-editing-tools-for-clippers-india','Choose editing tools around your device, captions, export needs and the campaign’s requirements.','Choose a clipping editor that works reliably on your device and supports the captions, audio and exports your brief needs. Compare cost, availability, commercial-use terms and how easily you can make revisions. Test a small edit before committing. Choose a workflow you can use consistently and revise without difficulty.'],
 ['creator-clipping-campaign-guide-india','Plan the content, audience, review process and payment rules for your first clipping campaign.','Start a creator clipping campaign with a clear goal, an audience and videos you have permission to use. Agree the formats, publishing accounts, review process, budget and payment rules before editing begins. Review a small first batch, record the results you can verify and use those findings to decide the next step.'],
 ['creator-content-library-guide-india','Organise approved videos, timestamps, permissions and context so editors can find usable moments.','A useful creator content library gives editors approved videos, clear links, relevant timestamps and the context needed to avoid misleading cuts. Record permissions and restrictions alongside each source. Keep updates easy to find and remove access when needed. This helps the team edit from the same material instead of guessing which files are allowed.'],
 ['tiktok-clipper-guide-india','Check TikTok access, the intended market and publishing permissions before planning a campaign.','An India-based TikTok clipping plan must first address access, the intended market and who is authorised to publish. Do not assume a campaign can run like an Instagram or YouTube campaign. Confirm current platform and local restrictions, source rights and account arrangements before editing. This guide does not provide ways to bypass restrictions.'],
 ['youtube-shorts-clipper-guide-india','Make Shorts with clear context, accurate captions and a publishing plan that respects source rights.','For YouTube Shorts clipping, choose a moment that makes sense on its own and preserve the speaker’s meaning. Check source permission, captions, music and the publishing account before uploading. Campaign approval and YouTube monetisation are separate matters. Read the current brief and platform rules rather than assuming a permitted clip will earn ad revenue.'],
 ['instagram-reels-clipper-guide-india','Choose a useful moment, make it readable on mobile and check permissions and disclosure before posting.','An Instagram Reel should give viewers a clear reason to watch and enough context to understand the moment. Keep the subject and captions readable on mobile. Confirm source rights, music use, publishing permissions and any advertising disclosure. Measure what you can access honestly; views alone do not establish campaign payment or sales.'],
 ['x-twitter-clipper-guide-india','Plan video context, captions, account permissions and the post that accompanies each clip on X.','When clipping for X, treat the video and its accompanying post as one message. Preserve source context, add readable captions and use a clear account identity. Confirm permission to publish and any required advertising disclosure. Agree the campaign’s accepted metrics and payment rules rather than assuming every public view will count.'],
 ['podcast-clipping-guide-india','Find a complete answer inside a podcast and keep the context, captions and next viewing step clear.','A useful podcast clip contains a question, insight or story viewers can understand without hearing the whole episode. Keep qualifications and necessary context, then add accurate captions and a clear link to the full conversation where appropriate. Confirm guest, footage and music permissions before publishing. Give viewers a clear next step to the full episode.'],
 ['stream-clipper-guide-india','Keep the setup and payoff together while checking the streamer’s permissions and platform rules.','A stream clip works best when viewers can understand what happened and why it matters. Keep enough setup for the payoff, make the crop readable and check rights to music or other material in the stream. Confirm the streamer’s sharing rules and campaign terms before posting through a separate account.'],
 ['creator-clipping-india-operating-manual-2026','A complete workflow for campaign planning, sources, submissions, review, measurement and payments.','Running a creator clipping campaign in India means coordinating more than edits. Agree source rights, audience, publishing rules, review responsibilities and payment conditions. Keep a shared brief and a record of submissions, decisions and measured results. Use this manual to plan the full workflow and resolve unclear steps before work begins.'],
 ['creator-clipping-campaign-roi-calculator-india','Use your own costs, eligible views and supported revenue figures to estimate campaign ROI.','This calculator estimates campaign ROI and cost per 1,000 eligible views using figures you enter. Include the full campaign cost and revenue you can reasonably connect to the campaign through a documented method. It starts empty and does not predict views, prove the campaign caused sales or confirm a financial return.'],
 ['creator-clipping-brief-template-india','Build a clear campaign brief covering sources, audience, deliverables, reviews and payment conditions.','A clipping brief explains what to make, which sources are allowed, who it is for and how work will be reviewed and paid. Use the blank builder to record your own plan, then copy or download it. Creating a draft does not send an enquiry or start a campaign. Review and share it separately.'],
 ['how-riseklix-verifies-clip-views-public-links','Understand what public links and dated metric records can show, and where their limits remain.','A public clip link helps a reviewer inspect the post and record the metrics visible at a stated time. It cannot by itself prove unique viewers, organic traffic or sales. Keep the link, observation time and review decision together. Confirm which checks are available for your campaign; do not describe missing information as verified.'],
 ['discord-clipping-server-setup-advanced-operator-guide','Organise campaign channels, permissions, brief updates and review records without losing important decisions.','A well-run clipping Discord server makes the current brief, rules and submission process easy to find. Assign clear permissions and review responsibilities, record brief changes and keep private payment details out of public channels. Start with a manageable submission batch. A busy server is not a substitute for a clear campaign process.'],
 ['clipper-verification-checklist-india','Check source rights, publishing accounts, submission records and the metric used for payment.','Before approving clipping work, check the source permission, required account, published link or file, captions, disclosure and deadline against the brief. Record what you inspected and any information you could not access. Keep approval and payment confirmation separate. This checklist supports consistent reviews; it does not prove every traffic source is genuine.'],
 ['creator-clipping-vs-influencer-marketing-india','Compare editing existing videos with commissioning influencer content, including ownership and measurement.','Clipping repurposes approved source videos; influencer marketing commissions content or promotion through an influencer. Choose based on the audience, available content, publishing accounts and result you want to measure. Both need clear rights, review and disclosure rules. Compare the full agreed scope rather than treating one model as automatically cheaper or more effective.'],
 ['creator-clipping-vs-paid-ads-india','Compare organic clip distribution with paid placement and decide what evidence each approach can provide.','Clipping and paid ads use different distribution methods. Clipping creates short edits from approved content; paid ads buy placement under an advertising platform’s rules. Compare the full costs, audience controls, source rights and measurement available. They can work together, but neither a view count nor an attributed sale alone proves the campaign caused the result.'],
 ['prevent-fake-views-clipping-campaigns','Set traffic rules, record what you can inspect and use a fair process for suspicious submissions.','To reduce fake-view risk, state which traffic is allowed and what evidence reviewers will check before the campaign starts. Keep dated metric records, investigate unusual patterns and let participants respond to specific concerns. Avoid automatic accusations from one number. Public metrics have limits, so report uncertainty and follow the written review process.'],
 ['asci-disclosure-guide-paid-creator-clips-india','Understand advertising disclosure and check how it applies to paid clips and publishing accounts.','Paid creator clips may need clear advertising disclosure when a material connection exists. Check the current ASCI guidance, the relationship involved and the platform’s requirements. Make disclosure easy to notice and understand; do not hide it in a long caption. Disclosure does not replace source permission or make an unsupported product claim acceptable.'],
 ['instagram-insights-clipping-campaigns-india','Read the Instagram metrics you can access and keep reach, views, visits and sales separate.','Use authorised Instagram Insights to understand the metrics available for the account and content format. Record the measurement window and distinguish views, accounts reached, watch behaviour and actions. Public counts may provide less detail. Keep website visits and sales separate from platform engagement, and do not claim access to private insights you do not have.'],
 ['youtube-shorts-analytics-clipping-campaigns-india','Understand Shorts metrics, record the reporting window and compare clips using the right definitions.','YouTube Shorts metrics measure different parts of viewing behaviour, and their definitions can change. Record the metric name, reporting window and account access you used. Compare like with like and keep views separate from engaged viewing, audience growth and revenue. A campaign’s payable metric must be agreed separately from the public view count.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-for-indian-podcasters','Turn complete podcast answers into clips and give interested viewers a clear path to the full episode.','For an Indian podcast campaign, choose complete answers or stories from episodes you are permitted to reuse. Keep guest context, accurate captions and the intended language clear. Decide where clips will be published and how viewers can find the full episode. Measure that next step separately from clip views.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-finance-creators-india','Keep financial explanations, risks and qualifications together when cutting long videos into short clips.','Finance clips need the conditions, risks and limits that make the original explanation accurate. Avoid cutting a qualified discussion into a promise of returns. Check the permissions, applicable advertising requirements and current rules for the content involved. Use a qualified reviewer where needed; an engaging edit does not make financial advice suitable for every viewer.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-course-creators-coaches','Choose useful teaching moments without changing the lesson or implying unsupported student results.','A course or coaching clip should answer a real learner question and preserve the conditions of the lesson. Use authorised teaching material and keep outcome claims supported. Link to a relevant lesson or course page rather than a vague promise. Check advertising disclosure where needed and measure enquiries or learning actions separately from views.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-saas-founders-india','Show a real product task, keep the demo accurate and connect the clip to a useful next step.','SaaS founder clips work best when they show a specific customer problem and how the product addresses it. Use an accurate demo, remove private data and keep limitations visible. Send viewers to a relevant explanation or enquiry page. Track visits and qualified enquiries separately; views alone do not establish new customers.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-music-artists-drops','Plan music clips around authorised audio, a release story and a destination listeners can use.','For a music release campaign, confirm permission for the recording, composition, visuals and platforms involved. Choose a moment that fits the release story and gives listeners a clear next step. Agree publishing and review rules before editing. Clip views do not automatically translate into streams, listeners or revenue.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-d2c-brands-creator-content','Use authorised product demonstrations, accurate claims and a clear path to the relevant product page.','A D2C clipping campaign should show a useful product question, demonstration or approved customer explanation. Confirm rights to footage, music and testimonials, and keep claims accurate. Link to a product page that matches the clip. Record views, visits and orders separately instead of treating attention as proof of sales.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-events-summits-webinars','Plan speaker permissions, useful session moments and a clear destination for event clips.','Event clips should preserve a useful point from a session without changing the speaker’s meaning. Confirm permissions for speakers, attendees, slides and recordings. Decide whether the next step is watching a session, registering or making an enquiry. Keep that outcome separate from views and check any private information before publishing.'],
 ['clipping-campaigns-gaming-streamers-india','Keep gameplay readable, preserve the moment’s setup and check rights before sharing stream clips.','A gaming clipping campaign needs approved stream sources, clear publishing rules and enough setup for viewers to understand the moment. Check game, music and third-party content requirements. Keep captions and gameplay readable on mobile. Agree which metrics count for payment; a popular clip does not itself confirm a reward.'],
 ['what-is-a-clipping-campaign','Understand how a campaign turns approved videos into short edits through a shared brief and review process.','A clipping campaign organises people to turn approved videos into short clips for a defined audience. The brief explains the sources, formats, publishing rules, deadlines, review and payment conditions. It can help repurpose content, but the campaign still needs appropriate permissions and useful edits. Reach, sales and participant earnings are not guaranteed.'],
 ['what-is-a-clipper','Learn what a clipper does, from choosing the moment to captions, context and campaign submissions.','A clipper finds useful moments in longer videos and turns them into short edits. The work may include selecting the source, cropping, adding captions and preparing a submission for review. The exact role depends on the brief. Permission to use the content, publishing rules and payment conditions should be confirmed before working.'],
 ['what-is-a-creator-performance-network','Understand the people, campaign rules and review process behind a creator performance network.','A creator performance network coordinates creators, editors or publishers around a campaign with agreed rules and measurable activity. Responsibilities and payment models vary. Ask who supplies the content, who reviews work and which results count. The label alone does not prove performance, paid opportunities or a particular technology.'],
 ['how-do-clipping-campaigns-pay-talent','Understand fixed fees, approved-edit payments and view-based rewards before accepting a brief.','Clipping campaigns can use fixed fees, payments for approved edits or rewards based on an agreed metric. Before accepting work, confirm the rate, eligible submissions or views, caps, fees and payment schedule. Track estimated, approved and paid amounts separately. Joining a campaign or posting a clip does not itself confirm payment.'],
 ['how-many-clips-should-a-creator-campaign-start-with','Choose a first batch you can review properly, then use the results to decide whether to expand.','Start with a batch small enough for your team to review and measure properly. The right number depends on the sources, formats, budget and reviewer availability. Define the questions the first batch should answer, check recurring mistakes and adjust the brief before increasing volume. There is no universal clip count that guarantees success.'],
 ['what-counts-as-an-approved-clip','Check the brief’s requirements for source rights, editing, publishing and submission records.','An approved clip is one that passes the campaign’s written review rules. These may cover source rights, meaning, captions, format, account, disclosure, deadline and submission details. Keep the decision and any feedback in the campaign record. Approval does not automatically confirm a payable view total or that payment has been made.'],
 ['good-clip-submission-format','Send the reviewer a clear record of the source, edit, publishing link and required campaign details.','A good clip submission lets the reviewer find the work and check it against the brief. Include the campaign name, source link and timestamp, file or public post link, publishing account and required caption or disclosure details. Add the upload time where requested. Keep private payment information in the agreed private process.'],
 ['how-long-should-short-form-clip-be-india','Choose a length that keeps the point complete, fits the platform and respects the campaign brief.','A short clip should be long enough to make its point without losing necessary context. Start with the idea and audience, then check the platform’s current format limits and the campaign brief. Remove repetition rather than important qualifications. There is no single duration that guarantees better reach across all Indian audiences.'],
 ['what-is-a-clipping-network-india','Understand how a network connects campaign organisers, approved content and people who make clips.','A clipping network in India connects campaign organisers with people who edit or publish approved short clips. A useful network provides clear briefs, review rules, permissions and payment conditions. It may operate through Discord, software or both. Its size alone does not confirm work quality, available campaigns or earnings.'],
 ['how-riseklix-is-building-indias-clipper-layer','Read the intended RiseKlix workflow and understand which campaign details still need confirmation.','RiseKlix’s approach is to connect approved content, a clear brief and human review through a managed, Discord-first clipping network. This guide explains the intended workflow, not a measured claim about market size or campaign success. Ask the team about current availability, responsibilities and payment terms before planning a campaign or starting work.'],
 ['best-clipping-platforms-for-indian-creators','Compare current providers against your content, audience, review needs and payment arrangements.','Indian creators should compare clipping options by the work they need managed. Check source rights, platform support, language, review responsibilities, budget and payment arrangements. Confirm current offers directly and ask how results are recorded. This guide provides criteria for choosing, rather than a verified ranking or a promise of campaign performance.'],
 ['clipping-net-alternative-india','Compare alternatives to Clipping.net using confirmed campaign rules, support and payment conditions.','To choose a Clipping.net alternative in India, decide whether you need campaign management, editing opportunities or publishing tools. Compare permissions, review, costs, payment rules and support for the actual offer. RiseKlix is a managed-network option to discuss. Confirm current availability and terms rather than choosing from a name or an earnings claim alone.'],
 ['whop-clips-alternative-india','Check the specific offer, responsibilities and payment rules when comparing Whop clipping alternatives.','Whop clipping alternatives should be compared with the particular product or community you are considering, since offers can differ. Check approved sources, who reviews work, fees, payment support and dispute handling. RiseKlix uses a managed, Discord-first workflow. Confirm the campaign details directly; an alternative listing is not a guarantee of work.'],
 ['vyro-alternative-indian-campaigns','Find the workflow that fits your Indian campaign and confirm its source, review and payment rules.','If you are considering a Vyro alternative for an Indian campaign, compare the full workflow: content permissions, publishing accounts, review, payment and support. Discuss RiseKlix’s managed-network scope with the team and verify the other provider’s current offer. Choose based on the responsibilities you need covered, not unsupported performance comparisons.'],
 ['makeclout-alternative-india','Confirm the provider’s current offer before comparing managed clipping options for India.','For a MakeClout alternative in India, check the current provider identity and offer first; the material reviewed here refers to Clouted. Compare the actual campaign scope, source rights, reviews, fees and payments with the alternatives. RiseKlix is one option to discuss, with availability and terms to be confirmed directly.'],
 ['how-to-plan-a-creator-clipping-campaign-india','Turn your campaign idea into a written plan for content, review, publishing and payments.','Plan a clipping campaign by choosing a goal, audience, language and approved source videos. Write down the deliverables, publishing accounts, review process, budget and payment rules. Start with a small batch you can inspect. Use measured results and reviewer feedback to decide what to change before expanding the campaign.'],
 ['how-much-do-indian-clippers-earn','Estimate from the actual campaign rate and accepted metrics rather than an advertised income figure.','Indian clipper earnings vary by the payment model, accepted work, eligible views, fees and caps. No national earnings average is established in this guide. Enter the agreed campaign terms into the estimator, then keep the result separate from approved or paid money. Editing costs and taxes can also affect what you keep.'],
 ['upi-payouts-for-clipper-campaigns','Confirm whether UPI is supported and how approval, fees and payment timing work for your campaign.','UPI is a payment method, not proof that a campaign has approved your work or funded a reward. Confirm whether it is supported, whose name the payment details must use and the agreed payment schedule. Keep sensitive information private. Check the rate, eligibility, fees and caps before estimating what you may receive.'],
 ['discord-server-setup-for-clipping','Make campaign instructions, questions and submissions easy to find in your Discord server.','A clipping Discord server needs a clear welcome route, current briefs, source permissions and a submission process. Separate announcements, questions and review records so decisions do not disappear in chat. Assign reviewer responsibilities and keep private payment data restricted. Test the workflow with a small group before accepting more submissions.'],
 ['clipper-rules-template-india','Write clear rules for sources, edits, publishing, review and payment before asking clippers to start.','Clipper rules should explain which content is allowed, what to deliver, where to publish and how submissions are reviewed and paid. Include deadlines, corrections, caps, fees and a route for questions. Use the blank template to record your own terms. A draft becomes useful only when the campaign team reviews and agrees it.'],
 ['youtube-shorts-clipping-for-podcasts','Choose complete podcast answers for Shorts and give viewers a relevant route to the full episode.','For podcast Shorts, choose one useful answer or story and keep the context needed to understand it. Check guest, recording and music permissions, then add accurate captions. Make the next step to the episode clear where appropriate. Track that action separately from views, and check YouTube’s publishing and monetisation rules.'],
 ['instagram-reels-clipping-for-coaches','Create a useful teaching clip while keeping the conditions and limits of the advice clear.','Coaching Reels should teach one specific point without cutting away the conditions that make it accurate. Use approved material, check any client examples and keep outcome claims supported. Add readable captions and link to a relevant lesson or enquiry route. Paid relationships may need disclosure; views alone do not prove coaching enquiries.'],
 ['founder-led-brand-clipping-guide','Turn founder explanations into clear answers to customer questions, with accurate demos and claims.','Founder-led clips should answer a customer question or show a real product task. Keep the explanation specific, the demo current and any business claims supported. Remove private information and choose a relevant next step. Report views, visits and enquiries separately rather than assuming a founder clip caused sales.'],
 ['music-artist-clipping-campaigns-india','Plan an artist campaign with authorised music, relevant visuals and a clear release destination.','A music artist clipping campaign needs permission for the audio, visuals and intended publishing use. Choose moments that fit the release and make it easy to find the artist or track. Agree review and payment rules with participants. Keep clip views separate from music streams, listeners and revenue.'],
 ['course-creator-clipping-campaigns','Use short teaching moments to answer learner questions and explain the next relevant lesson.','Course creator clips should help viewers understand a specific lesson or problem. Use authorised material, preserve important conditions and avoid unsupported learning or income promises. Link to the lesson or course information that matches the clip. Measure visits and enquiries separately from views, and check advertising disclosure where relevant.'],
 ['event-clipping-guide-india','Choose useful event moments while checking speaker, attendee, recording and slide permissions.','Before clipping an event, confirm who may use the recording, speaker material, slides and attendee footage. Choose a complete point and remove private information. Decide whether the clip should lead to a session, registration or enquiry. Record that outcome separately from views and keep the permission record with the source.'],
 ['podcast-clip-hooks-that-work-in-india','Write an opening that matches the actual podcast moment and gives viewers a reason to continue.','A podcast hook should make the value of the moment clear without promising something the clip does not deliver. Start with a useful question, specific decision or meaningful contrast. Keep the speaker’s qualifications and language natural. Test your own audience’s response; this guide does not establish a universal hook formula for India.'],
 ['hinglish-clipping-guide','Keep Hindi-English speech natural, captions accurate and the meaning clear for your intended audience.','Use Hinglish when it matches the source speaker and the audience you are serving. Do not force slang or translate every term into the other language. Check captions, names, pronunciation and meaning with someone who understands both languages. India’s audiences differ, so choose language from the actual brief rather than assuming Hinglish suits everyone.'],
 ['regional-language-clipping-india','Plan regional-language clips with reviewers who understand the speech, context and audience.','For regional-language clipping, choose the language from the audience and approved source, then use a reviewer who understands it. Check local expressions, names, captions and the speaker’s meaning. Keep translations and transliterations consistent. Do not treat all Indian audiences as one language group or publish an unchecked translation as an accurate edit.'],
 ['clipper-portfolio-guide-india','Show samples with clear permission, your editing decisions and an honest account of your role.','A useful clipper portfolio shows what you edited, why you chose the moment and how you handled captions and context. Use content you have permission to share. Label practice work and explain your role in team projects. Do not present invented results, public view counts or someone else’s edit as your own evidence.'],
 ['best-free-tools-for-clippers-india','Choose tools that fit your device and export needs, then check what their free plans actually include.','Free clipping tools can help you learn and build samples, but their plans, availability and commercial-use terms can change. Check caption support, watermarks, export quality and device performance. Try a small edit before committing to a workflow. Use authorised source content; a free tool does not grant rights to the videos or music.'],
 ['capcut-vs-vn-vs-premiere-for-clippers','Compare device support, availability, captions, exports and costs before choosing an editing workflow.','Compare CapCut, VN and Premiere against your device, required captions, export quality, revision needs and budget. Check current access and terms for India rather than assuming every app is available. Test the same small edit where access is permitted. The best choice is the tool that reliably meets your brief, not a universal winner.'],
 ['ai-tools-for-clipping-workflows','Use automated suggestions carefully and keep human checks for meaning, captions, rights and claims.','AI tools can suggest moments, captions or rough cuts, but a person still needs to check meaning, accuracy, source rights and privacy. Review the tool’s data terms before uploading content. Treat its output as a draft, not proof of quality or campaign results.'],
 ['clipping-campaign-fraud-prevention','Make traffic rules clear, preserve review records and handle suspicious results fairly.','Fraud prevention starts with written rules for accepted work, permitted traffic and evidence. Keep submission and metric records, investigate suspicious patterns and allow a response to specific concerns. Do not treat one unusual number as proof of misconduct. Document review limits and separate suspected issues from confirmed decisions and payments.'],
 ['disclosure-rules-for-paid-clips-india','Check advertising disclosure for paid clips and make it clear to the audience where required.','When a paid clip involves a material connection, advertising disclosure may be required. Check the current ASCI guidance and platform rules for the relationship and format. Make the disclosure noticeable and understandable. It does not replace permission to use the content or justify misleading claims about the product or service.'],
 ['brand-safety-checklist-for-clippers','Review context, claims, captions, private information and the brand’s written boundaries before posting.','A brand-safety review checks whether the clip preserves meaning, uses permitted material and follows the brief. Look for misleading claims, inaccurate captions, private information and topics that need specialist review. Keep specific feedback with the submission. A checklist supports review, but it cannot promise that every platform or audience will respond the same way.'],
 ['how-to-brief-50-clippers','Keep a large editing group aligned with one current brief, clear assignments and a shared review process.','To brief a large group of clippers, give everyone one current source library and written brief. Assign moments or angles, collect questions in a shared place and use consistent review criteria. Review a small first batch before accepting more work. The group size here is a planning example, not a claim about RiseKlix’s team.'],
 ['clipper-recognition-ideas','Recognise useful editing and reliable work with clear criteria, permission and honest labels.','Recognise clippers for accurate, useful edits and thoughtful revisions as well as the results you can verify. Explain the selection criteria and ask permission before featuring work. Keep community recognition separate from paid campaign rewards. Avoid leaderboards that encourage misleading hooks or artificial traffic, and do not imply a bonus unless it is agreed.'],
 ['first-campaign-scope-checklist-india','Agree the goal, sources, deliverables, budget, review and stop conditions before the first batch.','A first campaign scope should explain the audience, goal, permitted sources, deliverables, reviewer and payment rules. Choose a small first batch and a budget limit you can manage. State what happens to pending work if the campaign pauses or the brief changes. Put these decisions in writing before recruiting participants.'],
 ['clipping-for-saas-founders-india','Answer a specific customer question with an accurate product demo and a relevant next step.','For SaaS founder clips, start with a customer problem and show the product task that helps address it. Keep the demo version, limitations and claims accurate. Remove private data and link to a relevant explanation or enquiry route. Separate clip views, website visits, qualified leads and customers when reporting results.'],
 ['clipping-for-d2c-brands-india','Turn product questions and authorised demonstrations into clips that match the destination page.','D2C clips should show something a customer needs to understand, such as use, size, fit or a product limitation. Use authorised footage and supported claims. Make sure the linked product page matches what the clip shows. Track views, visits and orders separately; product attention is not itself evidence of sales.'],
 ['clipping-for-webinars-india','Choose complete webinar answers and connect them to a useful session, resource or enquiry page.','Webinar clips should answer a real question while preserving the speaker’s meaning and any important conditions. Check recording, speaker and slide permissions. Give viewers a relevant next step, such as the full session or a matching resource. Measure visits and enquiries separately from views, and remove private participant information.'],
 ['clipping-for-youtube-channels-india','Choose useful moments for Shorts while preserving source rights and a clear link to your channel.','For a YouTube channel, choose Shorts that answer a question or introduce a complete moment from approved content. Keep captions and context accurate and make the creator easy to identify. Check current platform rules, including reused-content requirements. Campaign approval, channel monetisation and audience growth are separate matters.'],
 ['clipping-for-linkedin-creators-india','Turn professional explanations into useful clips with clear context, claims and next steps.','LinkedIn clips should make a professional idea or product task easy to understand. Keep the explanation specific, preserve qualifications and remove private customer information. Choose a relevant next step and confirm source and publishing rights. Track enquiries or other business actions separately from views rather than assuming engagement means a qualified lead.'],
 ['how-to-track-clipping-roi','Record full campaign costs and use a documented method to connect revenue with the campaign.','To track clipping ROI, record the full campaign cost and define how you will connect revenue to the campaign. Keep views, visits, enquiries and orders as separate stages, and avoid counting the same order twice. Use the calculator for your own scenario. Attribution has limits and does not by itself prove the campaign caused a sale.'],
 ['what-makes-a-clip-go-viral-india','Understand useful moments, audience fit and clear editing without treating virality as a promise.','A clip may spread when the moment is useful, understandable and relevant to the audience. A clear opening, accurate captions and enough context can help, but no edit guarantees virality. Review your own audience’s response and the traffic you can inspect. Keep a high view count separate from meaningful audience growth or campaign sales.'],
 ['why-india-needs-clipping-networks','Explore the coordination challenges that a clipping network can help address for Indian creators.','A clipping network can help coordinate approved sources, editors, language needs and review rules. That may be useful when a creator or team cannot manage those tasks alone. This article offers an editorial view of the opportunity in India, not proof of market demand, income potential or guaranteed campaign results.'],
 ['future-of-creator-distribution-india','Consider how permissions, language, audience ownership and measurement affect future clipping work.','Creator distribution in India may involve more short-form formats, regional-language work and coordination across accounts. The useful question is how to preserve rights, context and a clear audience destination as workflows change. This article discusses possibilities and trade-offs; it is not a forecast backed by measured market or earnings data.'],
 ['does-clipping-work-in-india','Decide whether clipping fits your sources, audience and goal, then test a small campaign with clear measures.','Clipping can help repurpose approved content for Indian audiences when the source, language and editing fit the goal. It does not guarantee reach, income or sales. Start with a small batch and define what success would mean, such as relevant visits or enquiries. Use the results you can verify to decide whether to continue.'],
 ['clipping-campaign-pricing-budget-india','Build a campaign budget from the actual work, review time and payment rules rather than a fixed market price.','Clipping campaign pricing depends on the source preparation, editing, publishing, review and reporting included. Agree the deliverables, revision limits, payment model, fees and budget cap before work starts. This guide helps you scope a budget; it does not establish a national rate card or a RiseKlix quote. Discuss your actual plan with the team.'],
 ['is-video-clipping-legal-in-india','Check content rights, permitted reuse, music and privacy before publishing an edited video.','Video clipping in India needs a review of the rights and uses involved. Permission for a video may not cover its music, guest footage or every publishing account. Check the intended use, platform rules and applicable exceptions with qualified help where needed. Attribution alone is not permission, and this guide is not a legal clearance for your clip.'],
 ['how-to-check-clipping-campaign-legit-india','Check the team, written brief, source permissions and payment process before accepting a campaign.','To assess a clipping offer, identify the team and ask for a clear brief, source permissions, review process and payment terms. Check claims against records you can inspect and understand what is still unverified. Avoid treating an invite, testimonial or earnings screenshot as proof. No single checklist can guarantee that a campaign is legitimate.'],
 ['how-to-choose-clipping-agency-india','Compare agencies by the work they will do, the evidence they can share and the terms they will agree.','Choose a clipping agency by checking its agreed scope, source-rights process, reviewer responsibilities, reporting and payment terms. Ask for evidence relevant to your goal and understand its limits. Compare full proposals, including revisions and costs, rather than follower counts or unsupported rankings. A clear first-batch plan is more useful than a promise of viral results.'],
 ['ai-clipping-tools-vs-clipping-marketplaces','Separate editing software from services that help coordinate people, offers and campaign reviews.','An AI clipping tool helps produce or suggest edits. A clipping marketplace helps people find offers or participants, with responsibilities depending on the provider. They solve different parts of the workflow. Compare source privacy, review, publishing, permissions and payment needs. Neither automatic edits nor a marketplace listing removes the need for human checks.'],
 ['youtube-reused-content-rules-indian-clippers','Understand why permission to use a video and eligibility for YouTube monetisation are different checks.','Permission to reuse a video does not automatically make a YouTube channel eligible for monetisation. YouTube also evaluates its current originality and reused-content requirements. Check the channel and the contribution made by the content, not just whether you added captions. Campaign rewards and YouTube ad revenue are separate payment systems.'],
 ['utm-tracking-clipping-campaigns-india','Create consistent campaign links and understand what tagged visits can and cannot tell you.','UTM tags label campaign links so your analytics can identify tagged visits. Use consistent names, test the links and record where they were published. They do not measure every viewer or prove that a clip caused a sale. Keep tagged visits separate from platform views and account for missing or overlapping evidence in your report.'],
 ['accessible-captions-short-form-clips-india','Make captions accurate and readable, with useful sound information and a careful mobile preview.','Accessible captions should accurately represent speech and include relevant sound information where needed. Check names, language, timing, contrast and line breaks, then preview on a small screen. Avoid covering important video details or platform controls. Captions improve access, but they do not replace a clear edit or a complete accessibility review.'],
 ['clipping-campaign-case-study-evidence-template','Write a campaign case study that separates measured results, estimates, missing data and your actual role.','A credible clipping case study states the campaign scope, dates, sources, costs and method used to measure results. Keep observations separate from estimates and explain missing data. Obtain permission for client material and identify your role. Use this template to organise real evidence, not to invent campaign results or imply that views caused sales.'],
 ['video-clipping-vs-video-editing-vs-ugc-india','Choose between repurposing a source video, editing supplied footage and commissioning new creator content.','Video clipping selects and edits moments from an existing source. Video editing is a broader production task. UGC work usually commissions new creator-style content, with scope varying by agreement. Choose based on the material you have and the work you need. Confirm rights, deliverables, revisions, publishing and payment rather than relying on labels alone.'],
 ['instagram-reels-vs-youtube-shorts-clipping-india','Compare audience, format, publishing rights and the metrics you can use before choosing Reels or Shorts.','Choose Reels or Shorts by the audience you want to serve, your approved sources and the next step the clip should support. Check current format rules, music rights, account arrangements and available metrics for each platform. Compare results using their actual definitions. Neither platform is a universal winner for every Indian clipping campaign.'],
 ['creator-owned-vs-participant-accounts-clipping','Decide who controls the publishing account, audience destination, corrections and payment conditions.','Creator-owned accounts give the creator direct control over publishing and the audience destination. Participant accounts are controlled separately, so the campaign needs clear permissions, identity rules and a correction process. Agree payment and removal responsibilities before posting. Source approval alone does not establish every account’s right to publish, and neither model guarantees reach.'],
 ['utm-links-vs-coupon-codes-clipping-attribution','Understand tagged visits, code use and survey answers without counting the same sale more than once.','UTM links record tagged visits, coupon codes record use of a code and surveys capture a person’s stated discovery source. These methods can complement one another, but their evidence can overlap. Avoid adding shared orders into one inflated total. Explain missing data and remember that an attributed sale is not proof of an extra sale caused by clips.'],
 ['clipping-submission-rejected-fix-appeal','Find the exact rejection reason, check what you may correct and use the campaign’s review route.','Start with the stated rejection reason and the campaign’s agreed rules. Check whether the issue concerns the edit, source rights, account, link, deadline or payment metric. Correct what the process allows and keep the original record. Use the official review route for questions or an appeal; resubmission does not guarantee approval or payment.'],
 ['paid-clipper-test-assignment-scorecard','Scope a small paid editing test with clear deliverables, feedback and a separate hiring decision.','A useful paid clipper test has an authorised source, a limited deliverable, an agreed fee, deadline and revision boundary. Review source judgment, meaning, captions and how feedback is handled. Keep test payment separate from future hiring and label practice material honestly. This scorecard is an editorial framework, not a validated industry standard.'],
 ['clipping-campaign-landing-page-checklist','Make the page match the clip’s promise and help visitors take a clear, relevant next step.','A clipping campaign landing page should answer the question raised by the clip and offer a relevant next step. Check mobile readability, working links, the enquiry process and the claims shown. Test tracking without treating every visit as a lead. Confirm these basics before increasing distribution, and avoid promises the page or campaign cannot support.'],
 ['facebook-reels-original-content-clipping-india','Check Facebook’s current originality rules alongside permission to use and publish the source video.','Permission to use source footage and Facebook’s originality or monetisation requirements are separate checks. Review the platform’s current guidance and the contribution made by the edit. Captions or cropping alone should not be treated as guaranteed eligibility. Confirm publishing accounts and campaign payment rules independently from any platform monetisation decision.'],
 ['twitch-clips-permissions-campaign-guide','Check the streamer’s sharing rules and separate Twitch clip creation from permission to repost elsewhere.','A Twitch clip feature does not automatically grant every right needed to repost or use the clip in a paid campaign. Check the streamer’s permissions, music, third-party material and the intended publishing accounts. Preserve context and agree review and payment rules. Use current platform guidance and ask about unclear rights before distributing the edit.'],
 ['why-viral-clips-dont-build-creator-audience','Understand why clip attention may not lead viewers back to the creator, and what to measure instead.','A viral clip can attract attention without building the original creator’s audience. Viewers may not recognise the creator, find the source or want the next piece of content. Make the identity and destination clear, then measure relevant next actions where possible. Keep clip views separate from returning viewers, followers and full-episode viewing.'],
 ['youtube-tutorial-clipping-shorts-india','Turn a tutorial into a complete short answer while preserving prerequisites and a route to the full lesson.','A tutorial Short should help viewers complete or understand one specific task. Keep any prerequisites, warnings and steps needed to make the answer accurate. Use approved content, readable captions and a relevant path to the full lesson. Do not turn a partial demonstration into a promise of a complete result.'],
 ['b2b-webinar-clipping-qualified-leads-india','Connect useful webinar answers to a relevant enquiry route and a written definition of a qualified lead.','B2B webinar clips should answer a question your intended customer actually has. Preserve the speaker’s conditions and link to a relevant resource or enquiry page. Define what makes an enquiry qualified before reporting leads, then record the evidence you can access. Views and clicks alone do not establish qualified leads or sales.'],
 ['influencer-sponsored-content-clipping-india','Check reuse permissions, advertising disclosure, claims and the accounts allowed to publish sponsored clips.','Repurposing sponsored influencer content needs agreement on footage rights, publishing accounts, duration of use, claims and advertising disclosure. The original sponsorship does not automatically cover every new edit or destination. Keep the message and any qualifications accurate. Check the contract and current platform requirements before approving a clip for publication.'],
 ['restaurant-cafe-reels-clipping-campaign-india','Show a useful food or venue question with accurate details, filming permission and a clear visiting step.','Restaurant and café clips can answer practical questions about food, location, portions or the experience. Use authorised footage and check current menu, price and availability details before publishing. Obtain appropriate permission for identifiable people. Give viewers a relevant next step and measure enquiries or visits carefully; views alone do not prove footfall.'],
 ['real-estate-walkthrough-clipping-india','Keep property details, filming permissions and important qualifications accurate in short walkthrough clips.','A property walkthrough clip should show a specific feature without misrepresenting size, location, availability or the offer. Check filming rights, private information and applicable advertising requirements with the responsible team. Preserve important qualifications and link to accurate property details. A short edit is not a substitute for a buyer’s checks or legal review.'],
 ['fashion-product-demo-clipping-size-fit-india','Show size, fit and product use clearly while keeping measurements, claims and availability accurate.','Fashion demo clips should help viewers understand fit, measurements, material or use, rather than imply one result suits everyone. Use authorised footage and accurate product details, and preserve relevant conditions from the demonstration. Match the clip to the correct product page. Measure visits and orders separately; attention alone does not establish purchases.']
];
const introductions = Object.fromEntries(copy.map(([slug,dek,answer])=>[slug,{dek,answer}]));
if(Object.keys(introductions).length !== copy.length) throw Error('Duplicate plain-language introduction');
function applyPlainLanguage(articles) {
 for(const a of articles) {
  if(!introductions[a.slug]) throw Error('Missing plain-language introduction: '+a.slug);
  a.contentReviewedDate=a.modifiedDate||'2026-10-07';
  Object.assign(a,introductions[a.slug],{description:introductions[a.slug].dek,modifiedDate:'2026-10-08',languageEdited:true});
 }
 for(const slug of Object.keys(introductions)) if(!articles.some(a=>a.slug===slug)) throw Error('Unknown plain-language introduction: '+slug);
}
module.exports={introductions,applyPlainLanguage};
